    "https://recruit.ucdavis.edu/JPF07792": {
      "title": "Junior SpecialistApply nowto Junior Specialist",
      "description": "Junior Specialist (JPF07792) - AP Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Junior Specialist (JPF07792) Junior Specialist Apply now to Junior Specialist Job #JPF07792 MED:RADIOLOGY / SCHOOL OF MEDICINE / UC Davis Position overview Salary range: For Exempt: \"A reasonable estimate for this position is $57,000 at Step 1 or $60,700 at Step 2\". For Non-Exempt: \"A reasonable estimate for this position is $27.30/hr at Step 1 or $29.08/hr at Step 2\". Application Window Open date: August 25, 2026 Next review date: Wednesday, Sep 9, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Thursday, Sep 24, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Radiology, at the University of California Davis, School of Medicine, is recruiting for a full-time Junior Specialist. The Junior Specialist will contribute to scholarly research activities within the Department of Radiology under the general supervision of Dr. Andrew Hernandez. The incumbent will actively participate in publishable research by assisting with the design, implementation, analysis, interpretation, and dissemination of research findings while developing continued expertise in quantification of contrast administration and energy consumption in CT and MRI. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES I. RESEARCH (80% Effort) pending continued funding A. Conduct research in environmental sustainability and energy efficiency under the direction of the Principal Investigator. B. Assist with the design, implementation, and refinement of research studies, including data collection, analysis, interpretation, and documentation. C. Contribute to publishable research through literature reviews, preparation of figures, abstracts, presentations, manuscripts, and other scholarly products, with opportunities for authorship or acknowledgments, as appropriate. D. Collaborate with faculty, research staff, students, and other members of the research team while maintaining compliance with university and regulatory policies. E. Present research findings at laboratory meetings, seminars, or scientific conferences, as appropriate. II. PROFESSIONAL COMPETENCE AND ACTIVITY (10% Effort) A. Participate in seminars, workshops, laboratory meetings, and other professional development activities related to medical imaging and environmental sustainability. B. Maintain current knowledge of scientific literature and developments relevant to the research program. III. UNIVERSITY AND PUBLIC SERVICE (10 % Effort) A.  Participate in departmental service activities, laboratory operations, mentoring of undergraduate students, or other University and public service activities, as appropriate. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Basic Qualifications • Bachelor's degree (or equivalent foreign degree) in Medical Imaging, Radiologic Sciences, Biomedical Engineering, Biotechnology, Environmental Science, Public Health, Biology, Physics, Chemistry, Engineering, or a closely related scientific field. • Demonstrated interest in research through coursework, research experience, internships, laboratory experience, or other scholarly activities. • Knowledge of basic research principles, including data collection, analysis, and documentation. • Demonstrated ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. • Effective written and verbal communication skills. Preferred qualifications (other preferred, but not required, qualifications for the position) Preferred Qualifications • Research experience related to medical imaging, CT, MRI, environmental sustainability, healthcare sustainability, or energy efficiency. • Experience collecting, organizing, and analyzing research data in particular EMR, mPower and DICOM data. • Experience conducting literature reviews and assisting with scientific manuscripts, abstracts, posters, or presentations. • Demonstrated proficiency using Microsoft Excel, powerpoint, Python, and statistical  software (e.g., R, SPSS, SAS). • Familiarity with research compliance, human subjects research, or institutional research protocols. • Demonstrated ability to mentor or collaborate with undergraduate students or research trainees is encouraged. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Authorization to Release Information Form -   This form is required for all applicants applying to academic recruitments. Please see the Employment Disclosure Requirements webpage for more information. Download, complete, sign, and upload the form . Statement of Teaching (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ucdavis.edu/JPF07792 Help contact: amgranados@ucdavis.edu About UC Davis As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment To implement this process, UC Davis requires all applicants for any open search to complete, sign, and upload the form entitled, \"Authorization to Release Information\" into UC RECRUIT as part of their application. 